175ER c  2005Ca02: {+175}Er was produced in the projectile fragmentation of     
175ER2c  {+208}Pb beam at 1 GeV/nucleon using a 1.6g/cm{+2} thick Be target     
175ER3c  located at the entrance of Fragment Separator (FSA) of GSI. The        
175ER4c  particle-identification was built on even-by-event basis. The          
175ER5c  experimental setup also included two multi-wire proportional counters  
175ER6c  for position measurements; two scintillation detectors providing       
175ER7c  time-of-flight and position information; and additional two            
175ER8c  scintillators and an ionization chamber (MUSIC) for energy loss        
175ER9c  measurements. Measured E|g using four "Clover" type Ge detectors.      
