175YB c  1969Fu03: The 0.1 |mC {+175}Tm activity was produced via the nuclear   
175YB2c  photo reaction {+176}Yb(|g, p){+175}Tm by irradiation of 200 mg        
175YB3c  enriched Yb{-2}O{-3} at 30 MeV betatron of the University of Jena.     
175YB4c  The |b-decaying electrons and |b-delayed |g rays were detected with    
175YB5c  Ge(Li) detectors and an anthracene crystal, respectively. The          
175YB6c  lifetime measurements were conducted using a 2 mm plastic              
175YB7c  scintillator for |b particles and a thick stilbene scintillator for    
175YB8c  |g rays. Measured E|g, I|g, level lifetime. Deduced |b feedings and    
175YB9c  log {ift}                                                              
175YB c  1970Ja20: The {+175}Tm was produced by irradiating samples of          
175YB2c  Yb{-2}O{-3} and 100 mg enriched {+176}Yb in Yb{-2}O{-3} form           
175YB3c  employing a 25 MeV end-point bremsstrahlung spectrum of the Linac of   
175YB4c  the University of Ghent. The low and high energy |g rays were          
175YB5c  detected using a 0.44 cm{+3} Ge(Li)X-ray spectrometer and a 50 cm{+3}  
175YB6c  Ge(Li) detector (|g-tech), respectively. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced    
175YB7c  |b-feedings and log {ift}.                                             
