175YB c  1999As05: The excited states of {+176}Yb were populated via the        
175YB2c  deep-inelastic reaction {+154}Sm + {+176}Yb at a beam energy of 949    
175YB3c  MeV, using two stacked targets (each 0.5 mg/cm{+2} thick and enriched  
175YB4c  to 97.8% {+176}Yb) . An annular silicon-strip detector was used to     
175YB5c  detect the fission fragments. The emitted gamma rays were detected by  
175YB6c  the Gammasphere spectrometer with 55 Compton-suppressed HPGe           
175YB7c  detectors. Measured E|g, |g|g coin, |g|g(|q).                          
175YB c  1997Le11,1997Le10: The excited states of {+176}Yb were populated via   
175YB2c  the deep-inelastic reaction {+48}Ca + {+176}Yb at a beam energy of     
175YB3c  250 MeV and beam intensity of 2 pnA, using a target of {+176}Yb with   
175YB4c  an isotopic enrichment of 97.8% and a thickness of about 1 mg/cm{+2}.  
175YB5c  An annular silicon-strip detector with an inner diameter of 5 cm and   
175YB6c  an outer diameter of 10 cm placed 10 cm downstream of the target was   
175YB7c  used to detect the fission fragments. The emitted gamma rays were      
175YB8c  detected by the Gammasphere spectrometer with 36 detectors. Measured   
175YB9c  E|g, |g|g coin, |g|g(|q).                                              
175YB cL E$Least-squares fit to E|g's, assuming |DE=1 keV.                      
175YB cL J$Based on rotational structure.                                       
