175YB  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jin Wu$CIT=NDS 206, 1 (2025)$CUT=29-Oct-2024$              
175YB c  2005Nc01: Excited states of {+175}Yb were populated via neutron        
175YB2c  transfer reaction {+176}Yb({+136}Xe,{+137}Xe) at a beam energy of 750  
175YB3c  MeV and maximum intensity of about 1 pnA using an enriched {+176}Yb    
175YB4c  target of about 2 mg/cm{+2} thickness backed with a thick layer of     
175YB5c  Au. The emitted |g rays were detected by the AFRODITE spectrometer     
175YB6c  consisting of eight Compton-suppressed clover detectors and seven      
175YB7c  LEPS Ge detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g. Single-neutron transfer    
175YB8c  reaction                                                               
