175LU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jin Wu$CIT=NDS 206, 1 (2025)$CUT=29-Oct-2024$              
175LU c  2019Kr06: {+175}Hf was produced 0.0025-cm-thick Hf metal foil          
175LU2c  irradiated neutron flux. The |g rays were detected with                
175LU3c  high-resolution Ge detectors. Measured E|g.                            
175LU c  2015La25: {+175}Hf was produced via the reaction (n,|g) on a research  
175LU2c  reactor using both the natural content of isotopes and the one         
175LU3c  enriched to 13.9% of {+174}Hf. The |g spectra were measured by two     
175LU4c  coaxial HPGe detectors. Measured E|g, I|g.                             
175LU c  1988Si22: The radioactive isotope {+175}Hf was obtained in the form    
175LU2c  of hafnium chloride in dilute hydrochloric acid. The point source was  
175LU3c  prepared by evaporating active solution onto a thin layer of cell      
175LU4c  tape under an infrared lamp. The |g rays were detected by one high     
175LU5c  resolution intrinsic Ge detector. Measured E|g, X-rays. I|g. Deduced   
175LU6c  K-capture probabilities to the 433- and 343-keV levels.                
175LU c  1956Ha68: {+175}Hf was produced by neutron capture of {+174}Hf. The    
175LU2c  delayed |g rays were detected by the two-meter curved-crystal          
175LU3c  gamma-ray diffraction spectrometer. The electrons were detected using  
175LU4c  the beta-ray spectrometer. Measured E|g, conversion electrons          
175LU cG E$From 1956Ha68, unless otherwise noted.                               
175LU cG RI$Weighted average of 1988Si22, 2019Kr06, and 2015La25, unless        
175LU2cG otherwise noted.                                                       
