175LU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jin Wu$CIT=NDS 206, 1 (2025)$CUT=29-Oct-2024$              
175LU c  1971On02: The radioactive isotopes of {+175}Lu were produced via       
175LU2c  one-proton transfer reaction {+174}Yb({+3}He,d) using a 28-MeV {+3}He  
175LU3c  beam produced at a tandem accelerator and a target from the 96%        
175LU4c  isotopically enriched sample of Yb{-2}O{-3}. The reaction products     
175LU5c  were analyzed with an Enge split-pole type broad-range magnetic        
175LU6c  spectrograph at eight different angles. A NaI(Tl) monitor was placed   
175LU7c  in the target chamber to measure particles elastically scattered at    
175LU8c  |q=45{+o} with respect to the beam direction. Measured E(level), |s.   
175LU9c  Deduced transfer momentum L and spectroscopic factor by comparing      
175LUac  with DWBA calculations.                                                
