175LU    COULOMB EXCITATION            1981SK01,1978BR20,1959EL4225NDS    202511
175LU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jin Wu$CIT=NDS 206, 1 (2025)$CUT=29-Oct-2024$              
175LU c  1981Sk01: The measurement was first done using a 168-MeV beam of       
175LU2c  {+48}Ca from the Chalk River MP Tandem bombarding a target consisting  
175LU3c  of a 50 mg/cm{+2}-thick natural Lu foil (97.6% {+175}Lu). The recoil   
175LU4c  distance measurements were performed with a thin Lu foil, while thick  
175LU5c  Lu on Ag backing were used for the line shape measurements. The        
175LU6c  emitted |g rays were detected using two Ge(Li) spectrometers. The      
175LU7c  second step is to Coulomb excite the lowest two members of the         
175LU8c  ground-state band in {+175}Lu using a beam of 2-MeV protons from       
175LU9c  Queen's university's 4 MV Van de Graaff. The angular correlation       
175LUac  measurements were conducted by moving one detector, while the other    
175LUbc  one fixed serving as a monitor. Measured T{-1/2}(level). |g(|q).       
175LU c  1978Br20: (|a,|a') E=9.0 to 13.5 MeV. Measured d|s(elast)/d|s(inel).   
175LU c  1959El42: (p,p') (d,d') E=4.5 MeV.                                     
