175HF    130TE(48CA,3NG)               2004SC41,1995GJ01,1990GJ0125NDS    202511
175HF  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jin Wu$CIT=NDS 206, 1 (2025)$CUT=29-Oct-2024$              
175HF c  2004Sc41: High-spin states in {+175}Hf were populated via the          
175HF2c  fusion-evaporation reaction {+130}Te({+48}Ca,2n) at a beam energy of   
175HF3c  194 MeV, using a target of |?0.5-mg/cm{+2} enriched {+130}Te           
175HF4c  deposited on a |?0.2-mg/cm{+2} Au backings. The |g rays were detected  
175HF5c  with the Gammapshere spectrometer equipped with 101 Compton            
175HF6c  suppressed Ge detectors. Measured: E|g, I|g, |g|g coin, DCO ratio.     
175HF c  1995Gj01: Isomeric states were populated using a bunched and chopped   
175HF2c  beam pulses of 198-MeV {+48}Ca (2 ns wide and 198 ns apart)            
175HF3c  bombarding a 2 mg/cm{+2} {+130}Te target. The |g rays were detected    
175HF4c  using 30 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g      
175HF5c  coin. Deduced levels below 3.0 MeV populated by 35/2- at 3016-keV      
175HF6c  isomer.                                                                
175HF c  1990Gj01: High-spin K-Isomeric states were populated using a bunched   
175HF2c  and chopped beam pulses of 198-MeV {+48}Ca (2 ns wide and 198 ns       
175HF3c  apart) bombarding a 1.9 mg/cm{+2} tellurium target enriched to 99.3%   
175HF4c  in {+130}Te. The |g rays were detected using 30 Compton-suppressed Ge  
175HF5c  detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g coin. Deduced levels above 3.0 MeV  
175HF6c  fed from (45/2+) at 4636 keV and (57/2-) at 7455 keV isomers.          
175HF cG E$From 1995Gj01, unless otherwise noted.                               
175HF cG E(X)$Transition not observed, but inferred from coincidence            
175HF2cG relations. (1995Gj01)                                                  
175HF cG TI$From 1995Gj01. Total intensities, corrected for efficiency and      
175HF2cG internal conversion. Conversion coefficients for pure transitions of   
175HF3cG the lowest multipole order were used.                                  
175HF cG E(Y)$From 1990Gj01.                                                    
175HF cG E(Z)$From 2004Sc41.                                                    
175HF cG E(W)$Weighted average of 1995Gj01 and 2004Sc41.                        
175HF cG RI$From 2004Sc41.                                                      
175HF cG M$Assigned in 2004Sc41 from DCO ratios                                 
175HF cG MR$DCO ratios were measured from gates within the bands and assume     
175HF2cG that the 717-keV |g ray is an E2 transition in 2004Sc41.               
175HF cL E$From a least-squares fit to E|g's, by the evaluator assuming         
175HF2cL |DE=1.0 keV for integer values, |DE=0.5 keV for one-decimal-digit      
175HF3cL values, |DE=0.05 keV for two-decimal-digit ones.                       
175HF cL J$Based on rotational structure, |g-ray decay patterns, and DCO        
175HF2cL ratios in 2004Sc41, 1995Gj01, 1990Gj01.                                
175HF CL BAND(A)$5/2-[512] band                                                 
175HF CL BAND(B)$7/2+[633] band                                                 
175HF CL BAND(C)$K{+|p}=(9/2+) band                                             
175HF CL BAND(D)$K{+|p}=19/2+ band                                              
175HF CL BAND(E)$K{+|p}=21/2+ band                                              
175HF CL BAND(F)$K{+|p}=23/2- band. possible configuration:                     
175HF2cL |n7/2+[633]+|p9/2-[514]+|p7/2+[404]. (1995Gj01)                        
175HF CL BAND(G)$K{+|p}=35/2-, 5-quasiparticle intrinsic band. possible         
175HF2cL configuration: |n7/2+[633]+|n5/2-[512]+                                
175HF3cL |n7/2-[514]+|p7/2+[404]+|p9/2-[514] (1990Gj01).                        
175HF CL BAND(H)$K{+|p}=(39/2+), 5-quasiparticle intrinsic band. possible       
175HF2cL configuration: |n7/2+[633]+|n9/2+[624]+                                
175HF3cL |n7/2-[514]+|p7/2+[404]+|p9/2-[514] (1990Gj01).                        
175HF CL BAND(I)$K{+|p}=(45/2+), 7-quasiparticle band. possible configuration:  
175HF2cL (35/2-)+|n1/2-[521]+|n9/2+[624] (1990Gj01).                            
175HF CL BAND(J)$1/2-[521] band                                                 
175HF CL BAND(K)$Band based on 31/2-                                            
175HF CL BAND(L)$Band based on 79/2-                                            
