175TA  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jin Wu$CIT=NDS 206, 1 (2025)$CUT=29-Oct-2024$              
175TA c  1996Ko17: The high-spin states of {+175}Ta were populated via the the  
175TA2c  {+170}Er({+10}B,5n) reaction at a beam energy of 64 MeV, using an      
175TA3c  isotopically enriched {+170}Er metallic target with a thickness of     
175TA4c  about 4 mg/cm{+2}. The emitted gamma rays were detected with the       
175TA5c  CAESAR array, which comprised six Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors    
175TA6c  and an unsuppressed planar Ge detector (LEPS). Measured |g|g(t),       
175TA7c  |g(t), |g(|q). Deduced high-spin levels, J{+|p}, T{-1/2}.              
175TA cG E$Energies are accurate to within 0.1-0.2 keV for the strong, well     
175TA2cG resolved transitions. For other transitions the uncertainty may rise   
175TA3cG to 0.6 keV.                                                            
175TA cG RI(X)$Extracted from a prompt coincidence measurement.                 
175TA cG RI$From singles measurements, except as noted.                         
175TA cG MR$Extracted values from anisotropy data in 1996Ko17                   
175TA cG M$Assigned by evaluator based on A{-2} coefficient of |g(|q), except   
175TA2cG as noted.                                                              
175TA cL E$From a least-squares fit to E|g's, assuming |DE|g=0.5 keV by the     
175TA2cL evaluator.                                                             
175TA cL J$Based on the E1,M1,E2 multipolarities for gamma transitions (M2      
175TA2cL also if parent level has significant T{-1/2}) extracted from           
175TA3cL conversion coefficients and comparison of measured angular anisotropy  
175TA4cL coefficient A{-2} with theoretical values.                             
175TA CL BAND(A)$7/2+[404] band                                                 
175TA CL BAND(B)$5/2+[402] band                                                 
175TA CL BAND(C)$1/2-[541] band                                                 
175TA CL BAND(D)$9/2-[514] band                                                 
175TA CL BAND(E)$K{+|p}=(17/2+) 3-quasiparticle band. Possible config: |p{+3}   
175TA2cL [7/2+,9/2-,1/2-] or |p{+1}[9/2-]~#|n{+2}[7/2+,1/2-].                   
175TA CL BAND(F)$K{+|p}=(21/2-) 3-quasiparticle band. Possible config: |p{+3}   
175TA2cL [5/2+,7/2+,9/2-].                                                      
175TA CL BAND(G)$K{+|p}=(21/2+) 3-quasiparticle band. Possible config: |p{+1}   
175TA2cL [9/2-]~#|n{+2}[7/2+,5/2-].                                             
175TA CL BAND(H)$Band sequence I: feeds J=17/2 to 29/2 members of 1/2-[541]     
175TA2cL band.                                                                  
175TA CL BAND(I)$Band sequence II: feeds J=21/2 to 29/2 members of 1/2-[541]    
175TA2cL band.                                                                  
175TA CL BAND(J)$Possible 5-quasiparticle state, or member of the K|p=(21/2-)   
175TA2cL rotational band.                                                       
