175TA c  1972Fo20: The excited states of {+175}Ta were produced through the     
175TA2c  {+175}Lu(|a,4n|g) reaction at a beam energy of 39-50 MeV bombarding a  
175TA3c  10 mg/cm{+2} metallic lutetium target. The emitted gamma rays were     
175TA4c  detected with a 25 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector at 90{+o}, 110{+o}, 125{+o}  
175TA5c  and 150{+o} with respect to the incident beam. Measured E|g, I|g,      
175TA6c  |g|g coin, |g(|q), |a|g(t), T{-1/2}. Assignment of single particle     
175TA7c  configurations is based on the energy systematics of Nilsson orbitals  
175TA8c  in neighboring odd-A Lu, Hf and Ta nuclei.                             
175TA cG RI$Measured at E=50 MeV                                                
175TA cG E(X)$Partly {+175}Hf or {+176}Hf.                                      
175TA cG RI(Z)$I|g(342.3|g + 343.5|g)=39 {I5}.                                  
175TA cL E$From a least-squares fit to E|g's.                                   
175TA cL J$J|p assignments are based on rotational structure and |g-ray decay   
175TA2cL patterns. Quantitative information from |g(|q) was deduced only for    
175TA3cL the 1/2-[541] intra-band transitions.                                  
