175RE    161DY(19F,5NG)                1995BA51,1992KI06         25NDS    202511
175RE  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Jin Wu$CIT=NDS 206, 1 (2025)$CUT=29-Oct-2024$              
175RE c  1995Ba51: The excited states of {+175}Re were produced via the         
175RE2c  {+161}Dy({+19}F,5n|g) reaction at a beam energy of 106 MeV, using the  
175RE3c  targets of 0.6-mg/cm{+2} thick and about 1 mg/cm{+2} thick. The        
175RE4c  emitted |g rays were detected with NORDBALL array consisting of 20     
175RE5c  HPGe detectors and 60 element BaF{-2} innerball. Measured E|g, |g|g    
175RE6c  coin.                                                                  
175RE c  1992Ki06: The excited states of {+175}Re were produced via the         
175RE2c  {+161}Dy({+19}F,5n|g) reaction at a beam energy of 88-112 MeV, using   
175RE3c  the targets of 3.7-mg/cm{+2} thick and 0.8 mg/cm{+2} thick. The        
175RE4c  emitted |g rays were detected with the CAESAR array of six germanium   
175RE5c  detectors with BGO Compton suppression shields and a planar Ge for     
175RE6c  low energy |g's. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g coin, |g|g(t), |g|g(|q),      
175RE7c  |g-ray excitation functions.                                           
175RE cL E$From a least-squares fit to |g-ray energies assuming |DE|g=0.5 keV   
175RE2cL by the evaluator.                                                      
175RE cL J$Based on |g-ray angular distributions and rotational structure.      
175RE2cL Additional support for assignments of spin, parity, rotational bands,  
175RE3cL and Nilsson quantum numbers, comes from comparisons of the             
175RE4cL experimental gyromagnetic ratios (g{-K}) values deduced from           
175RE5cL B(M1)/B(E2) cascade-to-crossover branching ratios and the ones         
175RE6cL predicted by the Nilsson model (1992Ki06).                             
175RE CL BAND(A)$1/2-[541] band                                                 
