175OS c  1992Sc16: The parent {+175}Ir was produced by {+141}Pr({+36}Ar,2n) at  
175OS2c  E=175 MeV, using a {+141}Pr target of 2.3 mg/cm{+2} thickness. The     
175OS3c  emitted |g rays were detected with the |g/X and LOAX detector types.   
175OS4c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g coin. Detected Os K| x ray, |g rays, and       
175OS5c  511-keV annihilation radiation. Measured T{-1/2}.                      
175OS c  1992Bo21: The parent {+175}Ir was produced by {+32}S at E=210 MeV,     
175OS2c  using a 2.8 mg/cm{+2}-thick samarium target containing 88.6% of        
175OS3c  {+144}Sm and 4.7% of {+147}Sm. Measured E|g, I|g, |g-x ray coin.       
175OS4c  Measured T{-1/2} using Ge detectors.                                   
175OS cG E,RI$From 1992Sc16.                                                    
175OS cL J$From adopted levels.                                                 
175OS cL E$From E|g.                                                            
175OS cG NR$Normalization cannot be done due to the incompleteness of the       
175OS2cG level scheme                                                           
175OS cL T$From Adopted Levels, unless otherwise noted.                         
175OS c  $ 2010Wa02 proposed an isomeric state with T{-1/2}=33 s {i4} in        
175OS2c  {+175}Ir, which decays to {+175}Os followed by the 339-keV delayed |g  
175OS3c  rays. It is inconsistent with the g.s. decay suggested by this         
175OS4c  dataset.                                                               
175IR  P 0.0          (5/2-)            9 S       2              6711     17    
175IR cP QP$From 2021Wa16                                                       
