175IR c  2021Ha32: The parent {+179}Au was produced by the proton induced       
175IR2c  spallation of UC{-x} target with E=1.4 GeV protons. Selective          
175IR3c  ionization using RILIS at CERN followed by mass separation. Ions of    
175IR4c  interest transported to the Windmill decay station. Measured E|a,      
175IR5c  I|a, |a(t) using surface barrier silicon detector and E|g, I|g, |a|g,  
175IR6c  |g(t) using a low energy Ge detector.                                  
175IR cL E$From E|g and E|a, consistent with Figure 3 of 2021Ha32.              
175IR c  2004Ra28: The parent {+179}Au was produced by the |a decay of          
175IR2c  {+183}Tl produced with the fusion-evaporation {+144}Sm({+42}Ca,p2n)    
175IR3c  reaction at a beam energy of 195 and 200 MeV, using a target           
175IR4c  consisting of two (95% enriched) stacked, 500 |mg/cm{+2} thick,        
175IR5c  self-supporting {+144}Sm foils. The |a particles were detected with    
175IR6c  an 80x35 mm silicon strip detector. Measured E|a.                      
175IR c  1968Si01: The parent {+179}Au was produced by the {+168}Yb({+19}F,8n)  
175IR2c  and {+169}Tm({+20}Ne,10n) reactions. Measured E|a with Surface         
175IR3c  Barrier Silicon Detector. Deduced %|a branching.                       
175IR c  Other: 1986Ke03, 1968De01                                              
