175IR c  2019Gi11: The excited states of {+175}Ir were produced at              
175IR2c  E({+88}Sr)=381 MeV from the K-130 cyclotron at the Accelerator         
175IR3c  Laboratory of the University of Jayvaskyla, using a target consisting  
175IR4c  of 600 |mg/cm{+2} self-supporting {+92}Mo. Recoils were separated      
175IR5c  using the RITU gas filled separator and implanted into the DSSD of     
175IR6c  the GREAT spectrometer. Measured delayed E|g, I|g, |g(t) using a       
175IR7c  segmented planar HPGe detector and prompt |E|g, I|g, |g|g using the    
175IR8c  JUROGAM II array consisting of 23 EUROGAM clover detectors and 15      
175IR9c  EUROGAM phase one detectors.                                           
175IR cL E,J$As given in 2019Gi11. Authors state that statistics were lower     
175IR2cL than prior in-beam studies (1991Dr06), thus while their results are    
175IR3cL in agreement, they were not able to improve on the high-spin portion   
175IR4cL of the level scheme.                                                   
175IR cG E$2019Gi11 gives mainly rounded values, which they state are in good   
175IR2cG agreement with earlier results by 1991Dr06. The two additions to       
175IR3cG level scheme involve the 26.1|g and 45.2|g.                            
