175IR c  2010Wa02: The measurement was performed with E({+35}Cl)=210 MeV from   
175IR2c  NLHIRFL facility in China, using a He-jet tape transport system. The   
175IR3c  |g counting was done using x-ray HPGe detectors, one coaxial GMX, one  
175IR4c  planar and one Segmented Clover. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g coin,         
175IR5c  half-lives of {+175}Ir activity.                                       
175IR  L 0                              8.8 S     5                             
175IR cL T$from timing of 105.6|g of the decay of {+175}Ir in 2010Wa02.         
175IR2cL T{-1/2} was obtained as 13.7 s {I8}, but after fitting the decay       
175IR3cL curve with a double exponential, half-life of 8.8 s was obtained for   
175IR4cL the shorter-lived component. This activity is known from earlier       
175IR5cL studies with a half-life of 9 s {I2}.                                  
175IR  L 0+Y                            33 S      4                             
175IR cL T$from timing of 399.0|g from the decay of {+175}Ir (2010Wa02).        
175IR cL $The isomer is suggested by 2010Wa02 decay through 399|g to {+175}Os.  
175IR2cL However, the previous decay dataset of {+175}Ir to {+175}Os            
175IR3cL (1992Sc16) didn't report the decay from an isomer.                     

