175AU c  2001Ko44: The excited states of {+175}Au were produced via the         
175AU2c  fusion-evaporation reaction {+94}Mo({+84}Sr,p2n|g) reaction at beam    
175AU3c  energies of 380 and 385 MeV, using an isotopically enriched (> 90%)    
175AU4c  self-supporting target with a thickness of 700 |mg/cm{+2}. The prompt  
175AU5c  |g rays were detected with the Gammasphere spectrometer consisting of  
175AU6c  101 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors. The evaporation residues were   
175AU7c  transported through the Fragment Mass Analyzer (FMA) and implanted     
175AU8c  into a 40 x 40 mm, about 60-mm thick, double sided silicon strip       
175AU9c  detector (DSSD). Measured E|g, |g|g coin, |a-|g coin.                  
175AU cG E$The placement of transitions and levels was determined from the      
175AU2cG |g-ray coincidence relationships, and the relative intensities within  
175AU3cG a given cascade. (2001Ko44)                                            
175AU cL J$Based on the analysis of spectroscopic data on the daughter and      
175AU2cL grand-daughter nuclei, and systematics in heavier Au and Tl isotopes.  
