175AU c  2017Ba46: The {+179}Tl was produced through the fusion-evaporation     
175AU2c  reaction {+104}Pd({+78}Kr,p2n){+179}Tl, using a {+78}Kr{+15+} beam of  
175AU3c  358 MeV impinging on a self-supporting rotating {+104}Pd target with   
175AU4c  a thickness and enrichment of 745 |mg/cm{+2} and 92.25%,               
175AU5c  respectively. The evaporation residues of interest were separated      
175AU6c  from beam and unwanted reaction products using the gas-filled          
175AU7c  separator RITU and transported to the focal plane, where the HPGe      
175AU8c  GREAT spectrometer is located to detect the emitted |g rays. The       
175AU9c  isotopes of interest were implanted into a 300-|mm-thick double-sided  
175AUac  silicon strip detectors (DSSDs) placed in the center of the GRETA      
175AUbc  spectrometer, in which the decay products of |a particles were         
175AUcc  detected. Measured E|g, E|a, T{-1/2}.                                  
175AU c  2013An10,2010An01: The {+179}Tl was produced in two reactions. First   
175AU2c  reaction E(p)=1.4 GeV at ISOLDE-CERN, using a target of 50 g/cm{+2}    
175AU3c  {+238}U. The {+179}Tl was ionized to 1+ charge by the Resonance        
175AU4c  Ionization Laser Ion Source (RILIS) and mass separated by the High     
175AU5c  Resolution (HRS) and General Purpose (GPS) Separators. Second          
175AU6c  reaction E({+40}Ca)=232 MeV provided by the UNILAC of GSI, using a     
175AU7c  target of |?350 |mg/cm{+2} {+144}Sm, separated by the velocity filter  
175AU8c  SHIP at GSI. Measured E|g, I|g, E|a, I|a, T{-1/2}, yield using a       
175AU9c  single Miniball Ge cluster and a DSSD. Deduced J{+|p}, |a branching    
175AUac  ratio.                                                                 
175AU c  2002Ro17: The parent {+179}Tl was produced using a projectile of       
175AU2c  {+78}Kr at E=355 MeV (340 MeV at midtarget) bombarding a target of     
175AU3c  90.4% enriched {+202}Pb. The recoil residues were transported to a     
175AU4c  gas-filled separator and parallel-plate avalanche counters, finally    
175AU5c  implanted into a Si strip detector. The emitted |g rays were detected  
175AU6c  with the HPGe detector. Deduced T{-1/2}, corrected for random          
175AU7c  correlation rates.                                                     
175AU c  1998To14: The parent {+179}Tl was produced using a projectile of       
175AU2c  {+92}Mo at E=420 MeV (404 MeV at midtarget) bombarding a target of     
175AU3c  {+90}Zr. The recoil residues were transported to a gas-filled          
175AU4c  separator and parallel-plate avalanche counters, finally implanted     
175AU5c  into a double sided Si strip detector with 40 in horizontal and 40 in  
175AU6c  vertical. Measured: E|a, t, I|a.                                       
175AU c  1996Pa01:  The parent {+179}Tl was produced from heavy-ion             
175AU2c  fusion-evaporation reactions. The recoil residues were transported to  
175AU3c  a mass separator and implanted into a double-sided Si strip detector   
175AU4c  (FWHM|<20 keV). Measured E|a, parent and daughter T{-1/2}.             
175AU c  1983Sc24: The parent {+179}Tl was produced using a projectile of       
175AU2c  {+92}Mo at E=414-497 MeV bombarding a target of enriched (>95%) Rb-Mo  
175AU3c  isotopes. The recoil residues were implanted into an array of seven    
175AU4c  position surface Si detectors. The emitted |g rays were detected with  
175AU5c  the HPGe detector. Measured E|a, I|a.                                  
