175HG4c  transported to the focal plane of the RITU He-filled magnetic          
175HG5c  separator. The gamma rays were detected using JUROGAM array of 43      
175HG6c  escape-suppressed Ge detectors. The |a particles, conversion           
175HG7c  electrons and delayed |g rays were detected using GREAT spectrometer   
175HG8c  which consisted of a multi-wire proportional chamber, two              
175HG9c  double-sided silicon-strip detectors, a planar Ge detector, a clover   
175HGac  Ge detector and an array of Si PIN diodes. The energy loss and         
175HGbc  time-of-flight information from the particle detectors were used to    
