175HG c  2017Ba46: The {+179}Pb was produced through the fusion-evaporation     
175HG2c  reaction {+104}Pd({+78}Kr,3n){+179}Pb, using a {+78}Kr{+15+} beam of   
175HG3c  358 MeV impinging on a self-supporting rotating {+104}Pd target with   
175HG4c  a thickness and enrichment of 745 |mg/cm{+2} and 92.25%,               
175HG5c  respectively. The evaporation residues of interest were separated      
175HG6c  from beam and unwanted reaction products using the gas-filled          
175HG7c  separator RITU and transported to the focal plane, where the HPGe      
175HG8c  GREAT spectrometer is located to detect the emitted |g rays. The       
175HG9c  isotopes of interest were implanted into a 300-|mm-thick double-sided  
175HGac  silicon strip detectors (DSSDs) placed in the center of the GRETA      
175HGbc  spectrometer, in which the decay products of |a particles were         
175HGcc  detected. Measured E|g, E|a, T{-1/2}. Deduced J|p, |a branching ratio. 
175HG c  2010An01: The parent {+179}Pb was produced in {+144}Sm({+40}Ca,5n)     
175HG2c  reaction at E({+40})Ca=232 MeV with a production cross section of 140  
175HG3c  pb {I40}. The evaporation residues were separated by velocity filter   
175HG4c  SHIP at GSI, and implanted into position-sensitive silicon (PSSD)      
175HG5c  detector. Measured E|a, I|a, (recoil)|g coin, |a|g coin using six      
175HG6c  silicon BOX detectors, three time of flight detectors, a veto          
175HG7c  detector and a four-fold segmented Clover Ge detector.                 
